      description: "Methotrexate is a folate-antagonist antimetabolite and once-weekly inflammatory-arthritis DMARD that forms intracellular polyglutamates, inhibits ATIC, and raises anti-inflammatory adenosine signaling. Those polyglutamates persist and alter folate and purine pathways. In rheumatoid disease, accumulation of AICAR and increased extracellular adenosine reduce neutrophil, macrophage, and lymphocyte signaling over weeks. At higher oncology exposures, inhibition of dihydrofolate reductase and thymidylate/purine synthesis limits DNA production in rapidly dividing cells. This dose-context difference explains why the same drug can be a weekly DMARD, a chemotherapy agent, and a source of fatal daily-versus-weekly errors.",
